-- title:
--   Existence of a rescaled logarithm over p-adically complete rings
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal O$ be a commutative ring, $p$ a prime whose image in $\mathcal O$ is a non-zero-divisor, and suppose $\mathcal O$ is complete (and separated) for the $(p)$-adic topology, i.e. for the ideal generated by $p$. Let $d\in\mathbb N$ and let $F$ be a $d$-dimensional formal group law over $\mathcal O$: a family $F_i$, $i\in\mathrm{Fin}\,d$, of power series in the $2d$ variables indexed by $\mathrm{Fin}\,d\oplus\mathrm{Fin}\,d$ with vanishing constant term, whose coefficients at the linear monomials $X_{\mathrm{inl}\,j}$ and $X_{\mathrm{inr}\,j}$ are $\delta_{ij}$, and which satisfies the associativity identity, and assume $F$ is commutative, i.e. swapping the two blocks of variables fixes each $F_i$. Then there are $d$-tuples $F_p$ of power series in the $2d$ variables and $\varphi$ of power series in $d$ variables over $\mathcal O$ such that: (i) for every $i$ and every nonzero multi-index $m$, $\mathrm{coeff}_m(F_{p,i})\cdot p = p^{\deg m}\,\mathrm{coeff}_m(F_i)$, where $\deg m$ is the total degree, so that $F_p(A,B)=F(pA,pB)/p$; (ii) each $F_{p,i}$ has zero constant term; (iii) each $\varphi_i$ has zero constant term; (iv) the matrix of linear coefficients $\bigl(\mathrm{coeff}_{X_j}(\varphi_i)\bigr)_{i,j}$ is the identity; (v) for every $N$ and every $i$, all but finitely many coefficients of $\varphi_i$ lie in the ideal generated by $p^N$; and (vi) for every $i$, substituting $F_p$ into $\varphi_i$ gives $\varphi_i(A)+\varphi_i(B)$, where $A$ and $B$ denote the two blocks of variables.
--
--   This is the integral form of the logarithm of a commutative formal group law in the sense of Honda and Hazewinkel: the logarithm $f$ of $F$ exists over $\mathcal O[1/p]$, and $\varphi(X)=f(pX)/p$ together with the rescaled law $F_p(A,B)=F(pA,pB)/p$ is defined over $\mathcal O$, additive with identity linear part, and has $p$-adically convergent coefficients. It supplies the $(F_p,\varphi)$ data required by the deformation-theoretic statement [`Deformation.exists_algHom_baseChange_eq_of_forall_map_mem_fontaineKer_of_forall_ker_eq_torsionIdeal_zmodp`](thm.html#Deformation.exists_algHom_baseChange_eq_of_forall_map_mem_fontaineKer_of_forall_ker_eq_torsionIdeal_zmodp).
